senses.gloss:
1 अ॑नु adv. afterwards, then;
 as prep. w. acc. after (in all
its mgs), towards, along, over;
 by (distrib.), with regard to, in
consequence of.

अनुकर्ष m. ˚ण n. drawing on, attracting;
 inclusion of
a preceding in a subsequent rule (g.).

अ॑नूक्त a. recited, studied, heard;
 addressed (with a
sacred verse), named, called;
 n. = seq.

अनुक्रम m. order, turn;
 instr. & abl. in due order, in
turn.

अनुक्रमण n. methodical arrangement;
 f. अनुक्रम˚णी &
अनुक्रम˚णिका table of contents.

अनुगत a. gone after, followed, visited, occupied,
conquered;
 following, complying with, obedient;
 equalling, resembling
(—˚).

अनुगुण a. congenial, corresponding to, equal to (mostly
—˚);
 abstr. ˚त्व n.

अनुचर॑ f. ई going after, following. m. attendant,
servant (adj. —˚ f. आ);
 f. ई॑ maid-servant.

अनुचित a. unwonted;
 not used to (gen.);
 not suitable,
improper.

अनुज a. after-born, younger;
 m. a younger brother;
 f. आ॑
a younger sister.

अनुजात a. = prec. a. + born again, invested with the
sacred cord (also ˚क*);
 taking after, resembling (acc.).

अनुदात्त a. not elevated or high, low;
 spoken with the
low accent. m. the Anudātta or low accent;
 ˚तर m. the lower accent
(before an Udātta or a Svarita).

अनुदेश m. instruction, advice;
 the mutual reference of a
latter to a former element (g.).

अनुपदम् adv. upon the foot, immediately after (gen.);
 at
every step, i.e. repeatedly.

अनुपरोध m. non-hindrance or prejudice;
 instr. &
˚तस् without detriment or prejudice to, with the consent of (gen.).

*अनुप्रवचन n. the reciting or learning of the
Veda;
 — ˚नीय a. belonging to the learning of the Veda.

अनुबन्ध m. binding, attachment, connexion;
 (also ˚न
n.);
 continuance, uninterrupted series;
 consequence, result;
 cause,
motive, intention;
 appendage, esp. indicatory letter (g.);
 indispensable
element (ph.).

अनुबन्धिन् a. reaching far, lasting long;
 connected
with, resulting in (—˚).

अनुबोध m. perception, observation;
 *reviving a faded
scent.

अ॑नुमत a. allowed, permitted, approved, liked,
agreeable, pleasant;
 n. assent, permission.

अनुयोज्य a. to be questioned;
 to be commanded, standing
as the command of (—˚).

अनुरक्त a. coloured, red;
 beloved;
 attached or devoted
to, fond of, loving (acc., loc., or —˚).

अ॑नुरूप a. suitable, adequate, fit, worthy, like,
resembling (gen. or —˚);
 able, equal to, a match for (gen.);
 adv.
अनुरूप˚तस्.

अनुरोध m. ˚रो॑धन n. compliance, regard,
consideration;
 ˚रोधतस् out of consideration for (—˚).

अनुरोधिन् a. compliant, considerate;
 observing, having
regard for (—˚).

अनुवंश m. pedigree, lineage, genealogy;
 a. of equal
race, adv. according to the race.

अनुवाक्य a. to be repeated or recited;
 f. ˚कृया
invitatory prayer ((r.)).

अनुवात m. the wind that blows from behind;
 अनुवा˚तम् &
अनुवा˚ते to windward.

अनुविद्ध a. pierced;
 intertwined or set with, full of
(instr. or —˚).

अनुवृत्त a. round, full;
 also = अनुवर्तिन्;
 n.
compliance, obedience.

अनुवृत्ति f. sequence, continuance, esp. the continued
application of a rule (g.);
 conformity, compliance with (gen. or —˚).

अ॑नुव्रत a. subject to the will of another;
 obedient,
faithful, devoted to (gen. or acc.).

अ॑नुषक्त a. clinging to (loc.);
 connected or endowed
with (instr. or —˚).

अनुष्टु॑भ् a. shouting after. f. shout, praise;
 N. of a
metre.

अनुष्ण a. not hot;
 lukewarm, chilly, cold;
 abstr. ˚ता
f.*, ˚त्व n.

अनुसार m. the same;
 rule, legal precept;
 instr. according
to, after (—˚).

अनुसृत a. following, repaired to (acc.);
 followed,
pursued, gone through.

अनुस्मृत a. remembered (n. impers.);
 recorded, taught,
enjoined.

अ॑नून a. not wanting, complete, full;
 no less, no inferior
to (abl.).

अनूप॑ m. a moist country;
 water-basin;
 shore.
